// Script Variable NPC_DIALOG_NAME :
"P2394848235" "Penelope Mayhem"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3310451310" "Why... what happened to you...? Is this what... I could become?"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4138731136" "YOU did this, {HeroName}! I'll make you pay for this!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - FaultlineHeroes 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3295732525" "You've destroyed part of Faultline and showed your allegiance with Penelope Mayhem!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2412989556" "The press are all talking about your work, {HeroName}. They're all stirring about how <i>you</i> created Penelope Mayhem. This is something even greater than just defeating a hero, quite greater.<br><br>A hero could stand being defeated... they would simply bounce back, fight the good fight and all that nonsense. Oh, but now... now you've instilled <i>fear</i> that the heroes never knew existed. You've shown that you will not only defeat anyone that comes after you, but that you will <i>twist</i> them into a nightmarish version of themselves. It is a fate that could be considered worse than death, and far worse than defeat.<br><br>You've earned your reputation as a feared villain, {HeroName}, and I am quite glad to have been part of it, quite glad. There is only one last thing we need to do."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Vanguard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P196397231" "{HeroName}, hold on. Vanguard does not want a fight. <i>You</i> are not our enemy. We're here to negotiate.<br><br>We knew that Splice would figure out where our safehouse is, and so we received permission to make you this bargain. We will freely give you the money in this safehouse. In return, you will hand over the Praetorian war criminals to us.<br><br>If you refuse, we will use our forces to take you out instead of your allies.<br><br>What do you say?"
// Answer Text :
"P1196263607" "(Hand Mr. G and the others over to Vanguard.)"
// Answer Text :
"P2902848072" "(Fight the Vanguard)"
// Page Traitor Text :
"P1900130742" "Excellent choice, {HeroName}. Our operatives are moving in now to take in everyone that you've gathered.<br><br>The safe is open, and the money is waiting for you.<br><br>In the future, {HeroName}, Vanguard would ask that you leave us alone, as we do employ heroes <i>and</i> villains. We're here to keep this planet safe, and I believe you are too, deep down inside."
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"
// Page Fight Text :
"P1407234927" "I think it's going to rain tomorrow."
// Answer Text :
"P1443913718" "Try again."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - FakeMrG 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page KnowMrG Text :
"P752095628" "<color orange>The Vanguard Operative from earlier approaches you with a nod. However...<br><br>You remember that you were tricked once before by a shapeshifter, when Protean pretended to be Leonard. You look over the Vanguard Operative as he talks to you and notice odd quirks in his movement and speech. Most people wouldn't notice it, but you were tricked once before by a shapeshifter - which means, you won't be tricked again.<br><br>You can tell that it's Mr. G in front of you right now!</color><br><br>... and that's that. Do you mind if I tell you something, {HeroName}, on behalf of Vanguard?"
// Answer Text :
"P3592843242" "I do, -Mr. G-. (Attack!)"
// Answer Text :
"P651188171" "What is it? (Play Along)"
// Page Normal Text :
"P369816955" "I hope you find the money to your liking, {HeroName}. Vanguard wants nothing more than to ensure that the relationship between us and supers remains very high. We all need to cooperate if we're going to save this world.<br><br>Do you mind if I tell you something, {HeroName}, on behalf of Vanguard?"
// Answer Text :
"P3733956995" "What is it?"
// Page Continue Text :
"P3558684118" "We've seen many horrors in our time, ranging back to the Rikti War and to the possibility of future threats from space.<br><br>All Vanguard wants is for your cooperation and for you to leave us out of your affairs."
// Answer Text :
"P918193767" "And what will Vanguard do?"
// Answer Text :
"P4281724275" "You should stay out of mine then, Mr. G. (Attack!)"
// Page Listen Text :
"P1952622474" "Vanguard's concern only lies with facing threats that seek to destroy or take over our world from other dimensions. Longbow and Arachnos can have their petty squabbles; we're only concerned with that, and one other thing."
// Answer Text :
"P3674130881" "Not so fast, Mr. G. (Attack!)"
// Answer Text :
"P2788264603" "What's that?"
// Page Attack Text :
"P3447255354" "This world is full of super villains. They want to do evil things like take over the world."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MrGHostile 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2934966398" "<color orange>Mr. G is teleported away to a Vanguard prison before he can say anything to you. It seems like it will be quite some time before you hear from him or your other allies.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MrGFriendly 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P821644123" "{HeroName}, none of us could have expected this to happen. We all greatly appreciate your help in defending us, greatly appreciate it.<br><br>We will continue working in our warehouse; should you need any help in the future, please feel free to come towards us. Yes... do feel free."
// Answer Text :
"P1700039553" "I will, Mr. G."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1016715901" "I would like to propose one final attack against Vanguard, this time against one of their vaults that they keep in St. Martial. It was well hidden, yes, but Splice was able to find it. You <i>could</i> rob any regular bank around here, but why not go after the funds for Vanguard directly? It would be another show of power to the group, don't you agree?"
// AcceptString :
"P3708436419" "Sounds good, where is the location of this safehouse?"
// SendOffString :
"P218678297" "Here, I shall mark the location for you. It will be a simple smash and grab, yes, quite simple.<br><br>We will be waiting here for you to return with all of the loot, {HeroName}."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P751618300" "Rob Vanguard's Safehouse"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P573610094" "How are you progressing, {HeroName}?"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P4040864238" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: Choosing the Inevitible</color>"

